config W1_AML
	tristate "Amlogic W1 (W155S1 / AW3155) SDIO Wi-Fi and Bluetooth power"
	depends on MMC && CFG80211 && REGULATOR
	depends on ARCH_MESON || COMPILE_TEST
	help
	  Support for the SDIO side of the Amlogic W1 combo chip found on
	  Amlogic boards: the Wi-Fi itself, and the power switch for its
	  Bluetooth part. The chip brings its own MAC layer, so the Wi-Fi
	  driver talks to cfg80211 directly and does not use mac80211.

	  RF calibration is read at probe time through the firmware loader
	  as aml/aml_wifi_rf_<serial>.txt, falling back to aml/aml_wifi_rf.txt,
	  so those files have to be reachable in /lib/firmware.

	  Bluetooth runs over a UART and is driven by BT_HCIUART_AML, but
	  its core has no enable line and is powered through the chip's PMU
	  over SDIO, so it needs this driver as well. When the device tree
	  gives the SDIO function 1 node a "regulator" child, the driver
	  registers it, and hci_aml takes it as its vddio-supply.

	  Built from the CoreELEC w1-aml tree; this is vendor code, not
	  kernel-style code.
